Reason: the main draw loop looked every tile's depth up in the tile layer map (tile_layer_hide/shift state), about
2,250 hash lookups a frame in rm_a5h04. The list is sorted by depth, so neighboring tiles share a depth: the lookup is
kept from one tile to the next and forgotten at any other entry, the only place GML can run and change the map.
Upstream: Speed only, every platform. Retires this patch when merged.

